{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00430",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.08,
      "end_seconds": 7.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "hi there, is it alright if I come in now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.44,
      "end_seconds": 15.71,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "of course, put it down anywhere. So, how can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 19.73,
      "end_seconds": 26.89,
      "duration_seconds": 7.16,
      "text": "doctor, I've come along because I know the history, if it helps"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.56,
      "end_seconds": 31.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "absolutely, come and sit beside them"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.13,
      "end_seconds": 40.65,
      "duration_seconds": 7.52,
      "text": "It's blurry vision. I thought I'd wait, you know, but it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.95,
      "end_seconds": 48.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Which tablets or creams or inhalers do you use?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.46,
      "end_seconds": 58.42,
      "duration_seconds": 5.96,
      "text": "hmm, it's metformin, twice a day for my sugar"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.32,
      "end_seconds": 62.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.66,
      "end_seconds": 87.95,
      "duration_seconds": 24.29,
      "text": "500 milligrams. Amlodipine, 5 milligrams, once a day for my pressure. I take atorvastatin, 20 milligrams, at night for my cholesterol. Thyroxine. I take it it 75 micrograms, every morning. I'd been on rosuvastatin, not any more though, I stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.85,
      "end_seconds": 92.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "how long have you had it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.71,
      "end_seconds": 97.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "It's been three weeks, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.16,
      "end_seconds": 100.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "How much is it bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.55,
      "end_seconds": 107.07,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "maybe a four out of ten on a bad day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.68,
      "end_seconds": 114.95,
      "duration_seconds": 7.27,
      "text": "Uh, I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 115.05,
      "end_seconds": 121.47,
      "duration_seconds": 6.42,
      "text": "sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.55,
      "end_seconds": 127.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "later, thanks please go on what about constant thirst, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.76,
      "end_seconds": 143.44,
      "duration_seconds": 13.68,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, about a year. There's tiredness as well. Hmm, you know, I'd been passing urine a lot, but that went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 145.12,
      "end_seconds": 147.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Mm, that's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.8,
      "end_seconds": 153.9,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any foot sores or abdominal pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.72,
      "end_seconds": 158.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "no, none of those"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.17,
      "end_seconds": 164.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "A few quick ones: fever or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.71,
      "end_seconds": 170.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "No fever or weight loss, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.78,
      "end_seconds": 174.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "have you had any vomiting or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.57,
      "end_seconds": 178.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "No, no vomiting or chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.47,
      "end_seconds": 181.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.02,
      "end_seconds": 187.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "No, you know, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.74,
      "end_seconds": 191.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "On the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.4,
      "end_seconds": 201.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "my heart's been fine, as far as I know"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.35,
      "end_seconds": 205.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "right, are you working at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.25,
      "end_seconds": 210.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "Yes, I'm a nurse on a busy ward"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.35,
      "end_seconds": 222.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "any relatives with health problems I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.61,
      "end_seconds": 231.94,
      "duration_seconds": 7.33,
      "text": "my mother has migraines so, uh, my father had kidney stones"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.92,
      "end_seconds": 235.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "have you had any surgery before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.91,
      "end_seconds": 241.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Okay, so I had my gallbladder removed in 2016."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.2,
      "end_seconds": 245.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Do you have any known allergies at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 246.01,
      "end_seconds": 250.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "I don't have any known medication allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.62,
      "end_seconds": 263.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Is there anything medical in your background?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 264.64,
      "end_seconds": 276.03,
      "duration_seconds": 11.39,
      "text": "Um, I have diabetes, for about a year. I, I have high blood pressure, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.91,
      "end_seconds": 278.61,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "mm-hm"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.97,
      "end_seconds": 284.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Yes, high cholesterol. Yes, an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.5,
      "end_seconds": 293.97,
      "duration_seconds": 8.47,
      "text": "I see. Yes, high blood pressure and high cholesterol are known to us, good to have that clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 295.39,
      "end_seconds": 311.65,
      "duration_seconds": 16.26,
      "text": "doctor, I've got the readings for you blood pressure 171 over 103, BMI works out to 22.4, height 178 centimetres, saturation 99 percent, pulse is 78 beats a minute, respiratory rate 17, weight 71 kilos, temp 36.7 degrees"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.31,
      "end_seconds": 313.29,
      "duration_seconds": 0.98,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.12,
      "end_seconds": 317.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.86,
      "end_seconds": 322.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "A A little pressure here, tell me if it's tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.76,
      "end_seconds": 342.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "your feet look fine, no ulcers or sores, and the pulses are palpable"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.4,
      "end_seconds": 347.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "A little pressure here, tell me if it's tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 365.54,
      "end_seconds": 369.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "sensation to the monofilament is reduced on the right foot"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 371.85,
      "end_seconds": 391.19,
      "duration_seconds": 19.34,
      "text": "Right, you can sit back down. Having listened and examined, I'm honestly not certain yet. It It could be diabetes that isn't well controlled, or it might be a urine infection. A medication issue is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 393.01,
      "end_seconds": 400.07,
      "duration_seconds": 7.06,
      "text": "well, I've been thinking the worst, to be honest is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 401.4,
      "end_seconds": 420.56,
      "duration_seconds": 19.16,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with diabetes that isn't well controlled do well once it's treated properly. Let me just check I've got this right. You've had blurry vision for three weeks, and no chest pain or foot sores."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 421.37,
      "end_seconds": 422.07,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 423.43,
      "end_seconds": 427.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Have you had any tests for this so far?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 429.0,
      "end_seconds": 439.0,
      "duration_seconds": 10.0,
      "text": "I did have a urine protein test done last year, you know, but the the paper's at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 440.67,
      "end_seconds": 465.06,
      "duration_seconds": 24.39,
      "text": "Let's book kidney function tests to look into diabetes. I'm sending you for an eye check because of diabetes. What I'm giving you is glimepiride, 1 milligrams, before breakfast, until we review. It's for blood sugar control. Cut back on sweets, sugary drinks and white rice, and keep to regular meal times. I think a dietitian should see you too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 466.08,
      "end_seconds": 467.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Alright, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 468.26,
      "end_seconds": 490.5,
      "duration_seconds": 22.24,
      "text": "If it hasn't settled in a month, we'd think about an HbA1c, but not now. Keep an eye out, and and if you vomit repeatedly or become drowsy, call us the same day or go to emergency. I'd like you back after the results are back. Look after yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 491.77,
      "end_seconds": 496.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "that's everything I wanted to ask thank you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 498.31,
      "end_seconds": 499.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Bye for now."
    }
  ]
}